ian reports.","cites":["news:guardian:673df459e1c8"]},{"t":"2026-11-27T00:00:09Z","text":"Graham Paul Thorpe (1 August 1969 – 4 August 2024) was an English cricketer who played first-class cricket for Surrey and represented England in 100 Test matches.","cites":["wiki:rev:1385117141:0"]},{"t":"2026-11-27T00:00:17Z","text":"Graham Thorpe was born on 1 August 1969 in Farnham.","cites":["wd:Q3527096:P569","wd:Q3527096:P19"]},{"t":"2026-11-27T00:00:25Z","text":"Played for 2 clubs from 1988 to 2005: from Surrey County Cricket Club to England cricket team.","cites":["wd:Q3527096:P54:Q2725632","wd:Q3527096:P54:Q1321565"]},{"t":"2026-11-27T00:00:30Z","text":"Educated at Weydon School and Farnham College.","cites":["wd:Q3527096:P69:Q7990306","wd:Q3527096:P69:Q5436018"]},{"t":"2026-11-27T00:00:35Z","text":"2 awards on record, among them Wisden Cricketer of the Year (1998) and Member of the Order of the British Empire (2006).","cites":["wd:Q3527096:P166:Q3569447","wd:Q3527096:P166:Q12201526"]},{"t":"2026-11-27T00:00:45Z","text":"Graham Thorpe died on 5 August 2024 in Esher railway station, aged 55.","cites":["wd:Q3527096:P570","wd:Q3527096:P20","wd:Q3527096:P569"]},{"t":"2026-11-27T00:01:02Z","text":"The Guardian headlined it: “Graham Thorpe’s widow takes legal action against NHS trust after inquest”","cites":["news:guardian:673df459e1c8"]},{"t":"2026-11-27T00:01:13Z","text":"Sources: The Guardian, Wikipedia articles, Wikimedia pageviews and Wikidata. Every caption links to the evidence it rests on.","cites":["wiki:rev:1385117141:0","views:en:Graham_Thorpe:30d","wd:Q3527096:P569"]}],"time":"story","chapters":[{"t":"2026-11-27T00:00:00Z","title":"What happened"},{"t":"2026-11-27T00:00:17Z","title":"Born"},{"t":"2026-11-27T00:00:25Z","title":"A life across the globe"},{"t":"2026-11-27T00:00:35Z","title":"Recognition"},{"t":"2026-11-27T00:00:45Z","title":"In memory"},{"t":"2026-11-27T00:00:53Z","title":"Connected"},{"t":"2026-11-27T00:01:02Z","title":"In the news"},{"t":"2026-11-